From: Debian PHP Maintainers <pkg-php-maint@lists.alioth.debian.org>
Date: Sat, 2 May 2015 10:26:50 +0200
Subject: libtool_fixes

Refreshed for PHP 8.6.0beta1 (2026-08-13): upstream renamed the
AC_PROG_LIBTOOL call to LT_INIT and added two PHP_HELP_SEPARATOR /
PHP_CONFIGURE_PART lines just above it, which shifted this hunk's
context enough that dpkg-source refused it as fuzzy. The actual line
this patch removes, PHP_SET_LIBTOOL_VARIABLE([--silent]), is untouched
by that rename and is still present verbatim; only the surrounding
context lines changed. No functional change to what this patch does.

---
 configure.ac | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 57436a1..632c165 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1603,8 +1603,6 @@
 
 LT_INIT
 
-PHP_SET_LIBTOOL_VARIABLE([--silent])
-
 dnl libtool 1.4.3 needs this.
 PHP_SET_LIBTOOL_VARIABLE([--preserve-dup-deps])
